1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,565
Your boss arrives, and she has the right ships.

2
00:00:03,465 --> 00:00:06,860
But all she asks of the crew is, destroy everything,

3
00:00:07,310 --> 00:00:09,342
and she says nothing at all.

4
00:00:11,142 --> 00:00:15,298
Today she gets objectives of her own, a way to lose,

5
00:00:15,748 --> 00:00:17,954
and a third ship she's been holding back.

6
00:00:18,854 --> 00:00:20,876
Most of it is lines you already know,

7
00:00:21,326 --> 00:00:23,109
and one small part is a card.

8
00:00:24,309 --> 00:00:27,189
First, read how a Siege ends,

9
00:00:27,639 --> 00:00:29,381
because your objectives hang on it.

10
00:00:30,281 --> 00:00:32,946
In the Quest Log, on Helm's handheld,

11
00:00:33,396 --> 00:00:37,759
a Siege already has quests of its own, before any boss arrives.

12
00:00:38,659 --> 00:00:42,114
And here are the same quests in their file, four of them.

13
00:00:43,014 --> 00:00:45,233
The top one wins the game when it's finished.

14
00:00:45,683 --> 00:00:49,520
Under it is Break the Siege, which wants every raider gone,

15
00:00:49,970 --> 00:00:51,773
and two more that lose the game.

16
00:00:53,573 --> 00:00:55,327
Now look at your own objective.

17
00:00:56,227 --> 00:00:58,314
It says its parent is that top quest.

18
00:00:59,214 --> 00:01:00,464
So with Required on it,

19
00:01:00,914 --> 00:01:03,864
it's one more thing the crew has to finish before they can win.

20
00:01:04,314 --> 00:01:06,851
And without Required, it's a bonus.

21
00:01:08,051 --> 00:01:11,587
Here's my objective in the Quest Log, called Sink the Morrigan,

22
00:01:12,037 --> 00:01:14,419
but it's finished when every raider is gone.

23
00:01:15,319 --> 00:01:17,343
Let's make it honest, with two lines.

24
00:01:18,243 --> 00:01:22,534
The Objective line is the order the crew reads in the Quest Log,

25
00:01:22,984 --> 00:01:25,608
and Done when, destroy one morrigan.

26
00:01:27,408 --> 00:01:29,247
That last word is a role,

27
00:01:29,697 --> 00:01:34,703
and the Siege gives every named ship its own name as a role, in small letters.

28
00:01:35,603 --> 00:01:37,236
So whatever you wrote on the Named line

29
00:01:37,686 --> 00:01:39,842
is a word you can use here.

30
00:01:41,042 --> 00:01:44,346
Here's a second objective in the Quest Log, on Helm's handheld,

31
00:01:44,796 --> 00:01:48,957
for her second ship, with the Badb drawn in 3D at the top.

32
00:01:49,857 --> 00:01:52,437
In the file, it has no Required line,

33
00:01:52,887 --> 00:01:56,448
so it pays if they do it and it doesn't matter if they don't.

34
00:01:57,348 --> 00:01:59,615
Its description starts with the ship itself,

35
00:02:00,065 --> 00:02:02,697
the same key as on my Named line,

36
00:02:03,147 --> 00:02:05,660
and the words after it are her caption,

37
00:02:06,110 --> 00:02:07,697
which the game draws above her.

38
00:02:09,497 --> 00:02:11,020
After that comes a clock.

39
00:02:11,920 --> 00:02:15,133
Fails when, thirty seconds, which is a test number.

40
00:02:15,583 --> 00:02:17,743
Then Fatal, set to true,

41
00:02:18,193 --> 00:02:22,000
and a Lose line, with the sentence the crew reads when it's over.

42
00:02:22,900 --> 00:02:25,967
Use those three lines together, every time.

43
00:02:26,867 --> 00:02:29,505
And then I play it and I don't touch anything,

44
00:02:29,955 --> 00:02:32,004
and half a minute after she arrives,

45
00:02:32,454 --> 00:02:33,455
the game ends,

46
00:02:33,905 --> 00:02:36,026
and the end screen has my sentence on it.

47
00:02:36,926 --> 00:02:39,103
Then I set the real limit, ten minutes,

48
00:02:39,553 --> 00:02:41,413
and I say so in the objective,

49
00:02:41,863 --> 00:02:45,389
because the game doesn't warn the crew as the time runs down.

50
00:02:47,189 --> 00:02:50,199
And I give the Morrigan's description a page.

51
00:02:51,099 --> 00:02:56,174
Here's how the crew reads it in the Quest Log, and then the lines that make it.

52
00:02:57,074 --> 00:02:59,205
Her ship at the top, then the order,

53
00:02:59,655 --> 00:03:02,420
and a short list where each item starts with an icon.

54
00:03:03,320 --> 00:03:05,302
An hourglass for the ten minutes,

55
00:03:05,752 --> 00:03:08,209
and a skull for what happens when they run out.

56
00:03:09,109 --> 00:03:11,145
Lint doesn't read icon names,

57
00:03:11,595 --> 00:03:14,150
so copy them from the list on the page.

58
00:03:15,350 --> 00:03:18,171
Some things no line in a boss file can say,

59
00:03:18,621 --> 00:03:21,829
and a ship that turns up later is one of them.

60
00:03:22,729 --> 00:03:26,343
For those, a boss has one more line, called Hook.

61
00:03:27,243 --> 00:03:29,248
It names a block of script,

62
00:03:29,698 --> 00:03:33,045
and the Siege runs that block once, when she arrives.

63
00:03:34,845 --> 00:03:37,126
One hook comes with the game, so try it.

64
00:03:38,026 --> 00:03:41,798
And on Science, the biomech chip lists a swarm of them,

65
00:03:42,248 --> 00:03:44,075
with no script written by me.

66
00:03:44,975 --> 00:03:46,190
They aren't her story, though.

67
00:03:46,640 --> 00:03:47,912
So now we write her own.

68
00:03:49,112 --> 00:03:51,831
This is the one awkward thing in the lecture.

69
00:03:52,731 --> 00:03:57,048
Your boss file lives in common data, where an update never touches it.

70
00:03:57,948 --> 00:04:00,232
But a hook is script,

71
00:04:00,682 --> 00:04:03,832
and script has to be inside the Legendary Missions folder.

72
00:04:05,632 --> 00:04:07,849
So I make a folder of my own in there,

73
00:04:08,299 --> 00:04:09,369
with one file in it,

74
00:04:09,819 --> 00:04:15,200
named with two underscores, the word init, two more underscores, dot mast.

75
00:04:16,100 --> 00:04:18,786
I haven't changed any file that came with the game.

76
00:04:19,686 --> 00:04:23,125
But an update replaces that whole folder, mine included,

77
00:04:23,575 --> 00:04:25,459
so keep a copy of it somewhere else.

78
00:04:26,659 --> 00:04:28,068
Here's what we're making first:

79
00:04:28,518 --> 00:04:31,402
a red line on Helm, under the panel on the left,

80
00:04:31,852 --> 00:04:32,806
as she arrives.

81
00:04:33,706 --> 00:04:35,998
And here's the smallest hook there is.

82
00:04:36,898 --> 00:04:40,384
A label, which is three equals signs and a name.

83
00:04:40,834 --> 00:04:44,012
One line that says a sentence to every crew ship.

84
00:04:44,462 --> 00:04:45,886
And the line that ends it.

85
00:04:46,786 --> 00:04:50,145
Then the boss file names that label, letter for letter.

86
00:04:51,945 --> 00:04:55,673
Now there are two things to check, so there are two commands.

87
00:04:56,573 --> 00:04:59,240
The first reads my boss file, as always.

88
00:05:00,140 --> 00:05:04,207
The second reads all of Legendary Missions, my card included,

89
00:05:04,657 --> 00:05:05,921
the way the game will.

90
00:05:06,821 --> 00:05:08,486
Read the last line it prints,

91
00:05:08,936 --> 00:05:11,346
and you want it to say zero errors.

92
00:05:12,246 --> 00:05:14,986
The two warnings are in files that came with the game,

93
00:05:15,436 --> 00:05:17,665
so they're not yours and you leave them alone.

94
00:05:18,865 --> 00:05:20,707
Next comes a third ship of hers:

95
00:05:21,157 --> 00:05:23,295
ten seconds after the Queen,

96
00:05:23,745 --> 00:05:25,908
the Nemain arrives, here on Science.

97
00:05:26,808 --> 00:05:29,880
To make her, the card grows by four lines.

98
00:05:30,780 --> 00:05:34,106
A wait, which is one of your cards from Class 1.

99
00:05:34,556 --> 00:05:37,551
A line that stops if the game's already over.

100
00:05:38,001 --> 00:05:40,785
One long line that brings in a named ship.

101
00:05:41,235 --> 00:05:44,546
And your finish a step card, which sends a signal.

102
00:05:46,346 --> 00:05:49,834
On the ship line you change four things and nothing else:

103
00:05:50,284 --> 00:05:53,771
where she appears, her name, which ship she is,

104
00:05:54,221 --> 00:05:56,892
and her name again in small letters, which is her role.

105
00:05:58,092 --> 00:06:01,675
A signal finishes a step, and a step can reveal another.

106
00:06:02,125 --> 00:06:04,425
That's the chain from Class 1.

107
00:06:05,325 --> 00:06:08,710
So in the Quest Log, Her Reserve waits for the signal,

108
00:06:09,160 --> 00:06:12,283
and when it's done, Sink the Nemain appears in the list.

109
00:06:14,083 --> 00:06:15,848
Two things here catch people.

110
00:06:16,748 --> 00:06:21,739
In a boss file, the address after reveal is the key alone, with no slash.

111
00:06:22,639 --> 00:06:25,980
And the hidden step says, starts when revealed,

112
00:06:26,430 --> 00:06:29,159
and does not also say, state active.

113
00:06:30,359 --> 00:06:31,584
Run both of them again.

114
00:06:32,484 --> 00:06:35,118
And look at what a mistake in the card costs you.

115
00:06:36,018 --> 00:06:38,142
I'll take out one quote mark.

116
00:06:39,042 --> 00:06:42,152
Lint gives me an error that ends, mast compile,

117
00:06:42,602 --> 00:06:44,457
with the file and the line.

118
00:06:46,257 --> 00:06:49,794
If I played that, nothing in Legendary Missions would run.

119
00:06:50,244 --> 00:06:52,672
No Siege, and no other map either.

120
00:06:53,572 --> 00:06:56,270
Your Class 1 cards were in your own mission.

121
00:06:56,720 --> 00:06:58,476
This one's inside the game's,

122
00:06:58,926 --> 00:07:02,223
so run that second command every time you touch it.

123
00:07:03,423 --> 00:07:05,499
And now she arrives and says so,

124
00:07:05,949 --> 00:07:07,419
in red, on Helm.

125
00:07:08,319 --> 00:07:11,986
On Helm's handheld, three objectives are in the Quest Log,

126
00:07:12,436 --> 00:07:14,161
and the fourth isn't there yet.

127
00:07:15,061 --> 00:07:16,783
When I open Sink the Morrigan,

128
00:07:17,233 --> 00:07:20,545
there's her ship, the clock, and what it costs.

129
00:07:21,445 --> 00:07:24,389
Ten seconds later, there's the Nemain on Science,

130
00:07:24,839 --> 00:07:27,594
Her Reserve is done, and the fourth one appears.

131
00:07:29,394 --> 00:07:31,240
Then put the real numbers back:

132
00:07:31,690 --> 00:07:34,775
forty percent, ten minutes, and ninety seconds on the card.

133
00:07:35,975 --> 00:07:39,655
Your boss is now two things in two places.

134
00:07:40,555 --> 00:07:43,482
The file is safe from an update, and the folder isn't.

135
00:07:44,382 --> 00:07:46,356
After an update she's still in the list,

136
00:07:46,806 --> 00:07:48,993
and she arrives without her hook:

137
00:07:49,443 --> 00:07:51,495
no sentence, and no reserve ship.

138
00:07:53,295 --> 00:07:55,096
Lint tells you about it, too.

139
00:07:55,546 --> 00:07:59,594
It warns that Her Reserve is waiting for a signal nothing sends.

140
00:08:00,494 --> 00:08:02,157
So keep a copy of that folder,

141
00:08:02,607 --> 00:08:05,095
and put it back after every update.

142
00:08:05,995 --> 00:08:08,699
Next time is the last lecture of the class,

143
00:08:09,149 --> 00:08:10,936
and she gets a voice.
